<title>UK: UK traders bid for free-market grain, no details.</title>
<headline>UK traders bid for free-market grain, no details.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK grain traders placed bids for free market wheat and barley export refunds, the UK Intervention Board for Agricultural Produce said on Thursday.</p>
<p>But it was unable to give further details.</p>
<p>&quot;There has been an interest for wheat and barley but we can't give any further details,&quot; the board said.</p>
<p>--Jim Ballantyne, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8062</p>
</text>
